WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:03.436
Point of inflection.

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:05.405
I'm Michael Smerconish in Philadelphia.

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:06.406
A meeting in Germany

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:08.008
among Western defense officials

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:09.242
united against Russia's

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:10.944
invasion of Ukraine ended

00:00:10.944 --> 00:00:12.312
without resolution.

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:13.513
As to whether President

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:15.448
Vladimir Zelensky will get the advanced

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:17.550
battle tanks for which he pleaded.

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:19.419
This after Russia warned

00:00:19.419 --> 00:00:20.620
that if NATO's further arms

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:21.554
Ukraine with battle

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:23.390
tanks and long range missiles,

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.892
it will lead to a whole new level of war.

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:26.893
It's been nearly a year

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:28.261
since the Russian invasion.

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:28.962
The United States

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:30.997
perspective has shifted during that time.

00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:32.565
Remember the unwillingness

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:32.732
to be

00:00:32.732 --> 00:00:34.467
a participant in a three way deal

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:34.934
that would have had

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:36.669
the United States backfill

00:00:36.669 --> 00:00:38.538
Poland's fleet of fighter planes

00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:39.105
after Poland

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:41.241
gave MiG 29 fighters to Ukraine.

00:00:41.775 --> 00:00:43.843
The Biden administration said no.

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:44.344
Initially,

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:45.845
the administration was unwilling

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:47.347
even to acknowledge providing

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:49.549
Stinger anti-aircraft missiles.

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:50.784
But with the passage of time

00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:51.084
has come

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:52.085
a softening

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:52.685
of the Biden

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:54.988
administration's reluctance to go all in.

00:00:55.422 --> 00:00:57.490
Today, Ukrainian troops are in Oklahoma

00:00:57.624 --> 00:00:58.224
being trained

00:00:58.224 --> 00:00:59.592
to operate the Patriot Air

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:01.327
Defense System, which the U.S.

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:02.695
is now supplying.

00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:03.096
The U.S.

00:01:03.096 --> 00:01:03.930
is also providing

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.265
Stryker combat vehicles

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:06.966
to transport Ukrainian soldiers

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:08.401
on the battlefield

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:11.471
as part of a new and massive $2.5 billion

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:12.639
aid package.

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:14.507
And reports suggest a U.S.

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:15.942
willingness to greenlight

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:17.243
Ukrainian efforts to target

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:18.178
Crimea

00:01:18.178 --> 00:01:21.014
annexed illegally by Russia in 2014.

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:23.683
So what accounts for the change in U.S.

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:24.717
position?

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:25.518
Has the Western

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:26.653
objective changed

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:28.288
from giving Ukraine what it needs

00:01:28.288 --> 00:01:29.689
not to lose

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:30.890
to arming Ukraine

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:33.159
with what it needs to actually win?

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:34.794
And is our weapons supply

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:36.930
no longer tempered by concerns over

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:40.166
provoking Putin by crossing his red line?

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.469
My next guest says the latter

00:01:42.469 --> 00:01:44.604
is the wrong question to be asking.

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:46.806
Nigel Gold Davis is the former U.K.

00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:48.741
ambassador to Belarus, former

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:50.009
head of the economic section

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:51.845
of the British Embassy in Moscow,

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:52.912
now senior fellow

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:54.380
for Russia and Eurasia

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:56.015
at the International Institute

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:57.283
for Strategic Studies.

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.918
And the author of this recent piece

00:01:58.918 --> 00:01:59.886
in The Times.

00:01:59.886 --> 00:02:02.522
Putin has no red lines.

00:02:02.856 --> 00:02:04.591
Dr. Gold Davis A Red Line.

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:06.693
That's a trip wire for escalation.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:08.495
Why do you think it's flawed?

00:02:08.495 --> 00:02:09.796
Thinking to be guided

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:12.132
by an adversary's red lines

00:02:14.167 --> 00:02:15.001
Yeah, I think

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:15.768
that a red

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:18.771
line is a bad and unhelpful metaphor

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:21.741
in thinking about our policy towards

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:22.775
Russia.

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:23.810
It implies that

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:26.679
some special category of action

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:28.948
that if we undertake it,

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:31.117
will automatically in a trigger

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:32.152
like way

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:33.786
provoke some dangerous

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:36.189
and escalatory action.

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:36.990
In practice,

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:37.824
that's really not

00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:39.959
how international relations works.

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:41.161
It's not how we should be thinking

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:43.263
about Putin.

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:45.598
Putin wants to assert

00:02:45.632 --> 00:02:47.700
there are such red lines,

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.869
but his nuclear bluff in particular

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:51.971
has been repeatedly called

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:55.275
and shown to be empty since this war,

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:58.811
since his invasion began in practice.

00:02:59.078 --> 00:02:59.846
The actions

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:01.981
he will take at any given point

00:03:02.315 --> 00:03:04.651
will depend upon his assessment

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:06.853
of the risks and benefits

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:08.955
of doing those actions.

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:11.324
And he might claim he might threaten

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:12.959
that he'll do something.

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:16.396
Dangerous and radical against us.

00:03:16.396 --> 00:03:19.666
But in practice, what he does or doesn't

00:03:19.666 --> 00:03:22.735
do will be based on a practical calculus

00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:24.170
So our goal should be

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.838
not to deter ourselves

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:26.406
by fear

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:28.174
of what he might do,

00:03:28.174 --> 00:03:31.978
but to persuade him Putin that escalating

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:32.812
the war is

00:03:32.812 --> 00:03:34.847
radically against his own interests.

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:36.816
In simple terms,

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:38.551
are you saying that no longer

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.019
must we worry

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:42.121
that his response might be nuclear?

00:03:42.422 --> 00:03:44.224
If we do X, Y, or Z,

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:47.694
we should always be concerned

00:03:47.694 --> 00:03:49.495
about the possibility

00:03:49.495 --> 00:03:52.031
of nuclear escalation?

00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:55.368
It's not there's not a zero risk of that.

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:58.104
But our efforts should be focused

00:03:58.104 --> 00:03:59.939
not on wondering and worrying

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:02.008
about what might cause him to do that,

00:04:02.242 --> 00:04:03.843
but to persuade him

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:06.179
that under any circumstances

00:04:06.179 --> 00:04:08.982
he's going nuclear and breaking that

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:11.217
taboo

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:12.285
would invite

00:04:12.285 --> 00:04:14.821
disastrous consequences himself.

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:16.990
So we should be aiming to deter him

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:18.358
from going nuclear,

00:04:18.358 --> 00:04:20.226
not deterring ourselves

00:04:20.226 --> 00:04:21.194
from doing things

00:04:21.194 --> 00:04:23.896
that might cause them to go nuclear.

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:24.264
Dr.

00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:24.831
Gould Davis,

00:04:24.831 --> 00:04:26.566
has there been a change in Western

00:04:26.566 --> 00:04:28.101
thinking that initially

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:29.002
what we wanted to do

00:04:29.002 --> 00:04:30.403
was supply Ukraine

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:30.737
with what

00:04:30.737 --> 00:04:32.905
Ukraine needs to do to repel

00:04:33.139 --> 00:04:34.641
the Russian invasion

00:04:34.641 --> 00:04:35.375
to now

00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:36.175
given the strength

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:37.877
of the Ukrainian effort?

00:04:37.877 --> 00:04:39.512
Hey, they can win this thing.

00:04:39.512 --> 00:04:40.380
Let's give them what they

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.215
need to actually win the war.

00:04:44.284 --> 00:04:45.551
I think that's right.

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:46.419
And that's partly

00:04:46.419 --> 00:04:50.556
a consequence of the tenacity, bravery

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:53.960
and heroism and adaptability.

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:57.263
That Ukrainians themselves have shown.

00:04:57.263 --> 00:04:58.665
I also think there's now

00:04:58.665 --> 00:05:00.300
there's a growing recognition

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:01.367
that there's no

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:03.036
practical distinction

00:05:03.036 --> 00:05:05.138
between on the one hand

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:07.907
helping Ukraine to stave off defeat

00:05:08.241 --> 00:05:08.875
and on the other

00:05:08.875 --> 00:05:11.811
hand, enabling Ukraine to win.

00:05:12.612 --> 00:05:15.281
Anything short of a Ukrainian victory

00:05:15.682 --> 00:05:16.749
would ultimately mean

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:18.685
that Russia is better off

00:05:18.685 --> 00:05:20.186
and not worse off

00:05:20.186 --> 00:05:21.988
than it was at the beginning

00:05:21.988 --> 00:05:23.823
of this invasion.

00:05:23.823 --> 00:05:25.892
And that would be an intolerable outcome.

00:05:26.526 --> 00:05:27.927
It would show that

00:05:27.927 --> 00:05:30.129
flagrant aggression is rewarded.

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:31.998
That would be

00:05:31.998 --> 00:05:33.066
an object lesson

00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:34.534
to anyone else in the world,

00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:36.969
including China, watching this.

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:38.905
There's also no prospect

00:05:38.905 --> 00:05:40.940
that any outcome short

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:43.042
of a Ukrainian victory

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:44.510
and a defeat for Russia

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:46.479
would be a stable outcome

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:47.780
if this war was somehow

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.749
to end with Russia better off

00:05:49.749 --> 00:05:51.250
occupying territory

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:51.751
and also

00:05:51.751 --> 00:05:54.587
violating the people on that territory.

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:57.490
There's every expectation that Russia

00:05:57.990 --> 00:05:58.391
would, in

00:05:58.391 --> 00:05:59.359
due course,

00:05:59.359 --> 00:06:01.961
seek to launch a third invasion

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:04.230
after the first of 2014

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:06.566
after the second of 20, 22.

00:06:06.699 --> 00:06:08.701
So that would not be a stable outcome.

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:10.236
The only stable,

00:06:10.236 --> 00:06:11.771
durable outcome

00:06:11.771 --> 00:06:13.773
that serves Western security interests

00:06:14.006 --> 00:06:15.942
and international morality

00:06:15.942 --> 00:06:17.877
and international law at this point

00:06:17.877 --> 00:06:19.912
would be a defeat for Russia.

00:06:20.046 --> 00:06:21.948
But I think it's also very important

00:06:21.948 --> 00:06:22.415
for the West

00:06:22.415 --> 00:06:23.649
to send a message

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:26.219
to Russia, the message of reassurance

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:29.255
that if Russia will to retreat back

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:31.924
to its internationally recognized borders

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:33.826
no one threatens Russia,

00:06:33.826 --> 00:06:34.794
that will be a safe

00:06:34.794 --> 00:06:36.195
and stable outcome for Russia.

